  "description": "<p>fcrepo-camel uses jena classes for handling RDF in the org.fcrepo.camel.processor classes. Those should be swapped out for the corresponding clerezza libraries (<a href=\"http://clerezza.apache.org/\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://clerezza.apache.org/</a>), which wrap jena-core in an OSGi-safe way. It is possible to deploy fcrepo-camel without the change, but it would be significantly easier if its dependency chain was fully OSGi compliant &#8211; which would make the pom.xml configuration much cleaner.</p>",
